# Meetings domain

Source of truth: [`MEETINGS_PLAN.md`](../../MEETINGS_PLAN.md). Read it before implementing. Also follow [`feature-standards.mdc`](feature-standards.mdc).

## Visibility

- `TICKET_REQUESTER`: **403 on every meeting/requirement endpoint**; no sidebar nav.
- `meeting:read` / `meeting:manage`: `PROGRAMMING_HEAD`, `PROJECT_MANAGER`, `SENIOR_MANAGEMENT` only.
- `requirement:read`: above + `DEVELOPER`, `QA`, `SYSTEM_OWNER` (scoped).
- `requirement:create` / `triage` / `promote`: leadership + `SENIOR_MANAGEMENT` only.
- `SYSTEM_OWNER`: read requirements only — **no** `requirement:create` (use tickets).
- Unpinned requirements (`systemId: null`): invisible to non-leadership (`IN` excludes NULL).

## Never

- Hard-delete meetings, points, or requirements — archive only.
- Add `BACKLOG` or new `TicketStatus` — requirements are the backlog.
- Promote to anything other than **DRAFT** ticket — `PROGRAMMING_HEAD` approval still required.
- Promote without `systemId` on the requirement.
- Free-text `minutes` on `Meeting` — minutes are ordered `MeetingPoint` rows.
- Comment thread on meetings or points — only on **Requirement**; meeting-level attachments only on `Meeting`.
- Ship without capture, reorder, triage, and promote all working end-to-end.

